{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "A great way to extend rails functionality is by using Rails gems.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dfb58eca4bfad3a0975accafaef803c2cf821bac8fe03cb8e149ea676d8095f3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.94], [7, 1.94, 2.28], [8, 2.28, 2.4], [9, 2.4, 2.68], [10, 2.68, 3.02], [11, 3.02, 3.54]]}, {"text": "These libraries are easily plugged into existing ruby projects and allow for quick integration of complicated features.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c1873e82e9866baf2f300c89610a3729abfeac2f0f203d3b95d85c6213ed80ac.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.68], [2, 0.68, 0.92], [3, 0.92, 1.28], [4, 1.28, 1.56], [6, 1.98, 2.32], [7, 2.32, 2.58], [8, 2.58, 3.04], [9, 3.04, 3.4], [10, 3.4, 3.64], [11, 3.64, 3.84], [12, 3.84, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.44], [14, 4.44, 4.8], [15, 4.8, 5.26], [16, 5.26, 5.72]]}, {"text": "I noticed that for my side projects that are still growing, that I would like to be notified whenever a new user signs up, so I can reach out to them to get feedback on the product.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b49f10781712cbd98f1e1d912aa3b772efd0a4c3b5db7a881e4dafd71a4c0fbb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 0.9], [4, 0.9, 1.06], [5, 1.06, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.8], [7, 1.8, 2.06], [8, 2.06, 2.18], [9, 2.18, 2.4], [10, 2.4, 2.8], [11, 3.22, 3.3], [12, 3.3, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.54], [14, 3.54, 3.7], [15, 3.7, 3.9], [16, 3.9, 4.0], [17, 4.0, 4.42], [18, 4.42, 4.76], [19, 4.76, 5.06], [20, 5.06, 5.22], [21, 5.22, 5.58], [22, 5.58, 5.9], [23, 5.9, 6.24], [24, 6.56, 6.78], [25, 6.78, 6.86], [26, 6.86, 6.98], [27, 6.98, 7.14], [28, 7.14, 7.38], [29, 7.38, 7.54], [30, 7.54, 7.68], [31, 7.68, 7.92], [32, 7.92, 8.06], [33, 8.06, 8.34], [34, 8.34, 8.64], [35, 8.64, 8.76], [36, 8.76, 9.08]]}, {"text": "Here I will go through step by step on how I created Angora, email notifications on model creation", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ff1a7aeddbf3f7ea5d24b7ea8ad64b0d70cc406ec1948c3965f276a384f2c2cd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [2, 0.46, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.84], [5, 0.84, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.24], [7, 1.24, 1.56], [8, 1.56, 1.8], [9, 1.8, 1.96], [10, 1.96, 2.1], [11, 2.1, 2.5], [13, 3.34, 3.48], [14, 3.48, 4.16], [15, 4.16, 4.48], [16, 4.48, 4.68], [17, 4.68, 5.12]]}, {"text": "The art of naming", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/36f4a6469eadcb3cf3ea88e8de39afb222e7348ddf2fb11fe3a0221027315ff1.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.88]]}, {"text": "Firstly, select a name.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3bd08aeb0c8f94afd642db5327f6212c1d4b3231d17924f5ab3648c09799e920.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.6, 0.82], [2, 0.82, 1.0], [3, 1.0, 1.26]]}, {"text": "This name should be unique to other gems so other developers can easily find it.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/265b7c5cf16c9c954d9d1cc9892571b4aeb3310856d7b68e6f3c184a49d2dfc0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.08], [5, 1.08, 1.3], [6, 1.3, 1.48], [8, 1.8, 2.1], [9, 2.1, 2.36], [10, 2.36, 2.86], [11, 2.86, 3.16], [12, 3.16, 3.48], [13, 3.48, 3.84], [14, 3.84, 4.12]]}, {"text": "Check Github and RubyGems to verify that there aren’t any other gems with the same name.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/be12f5acb71c5b247ccaeae9e1e245c93dee08f8e6abbf50f05bec1c9c9703ea.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [2, 0.8, 1.1], [4, 1.68, 1.86], [5, 1.86, 2.16], [6, 2.16, 2.48], [7, 2.48, 2.64], [8, 2.64, 2.86], [9, 2.86, 3.04], [10, 3.04, 3.18], [11, 3.18, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.64], [13, 3.64, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 3.94], [15, 3.94, 4.16]]}, {"text": "RubyGems provides a excellent table for describing how to name a gem.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fb5d55c870bad642927806784d52f4328ef61f03337b2f77010888d6ca7031bb.mp3"}, {"text": "Creating the gem", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9817904bf3ced697c53e83c1f6d1425c8a9eeadd3169b73e2cff6880e02bb39b.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.38, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.86]]}, {"text": "We are going to use the bundler tool to generate the gem files.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/34790a0b1b268569c1f281fbe67c1f9d629cf77179782a39b16587b44ace4d8a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.86], [5, 0.86, 1.0], [6, 1.0, 1.34], [7, 1.34, 1.66], [8, 1.66, 2.2], [9, 2.2, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 2.78], [11, 2.78, 2.96], [12, 2.96, 3.34]]}, {"text": "Since my gem name is angora, I type this in:", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/33d7ca44e5565a247f540a8e9e27d489f011e0e6717aeae6bf7c754cab7c84b3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.84], [4, 0.84, 1.06], [6, 1.68, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 1.98], [8, 1.98, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.38]]}, {"text": "``` console Creating gem with bundler $ bundle gem angora create angora/Gemfile create angora/Rakefile create angora/LICENSE.txt create angora/README.md create angora/.gitignore create angora/angora.gemspec create angora/lib/angora.rb create angora/lib/angora/version.rb", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/19b180761675eb533b3d3fa69481462904fff1d113fd658fd28e29306d0bc0a4.mp3"}, {"text": "The basics", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4c61ef7bdac4fbd2e6c6f6b29ab3c93ea0f378260a802937c24f9143b660cbe2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.56]]}, {"text": "Now we are going to edit the basic attributes of angora.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7dcd861d81d32ce78d62c43a9792a2c6799ca5033de7dc6f9b5a4734f519dbbd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.76], [4, 0.76, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.12], [6, 1.12, 1.32], [7, 1.32, 1.66], [8, 1.66, 2.16], [9, 2.16, 2.42]]}, {"text": "Open up angora.gemspec to see all of the generated defaults.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b3986fd74231c3ae2974be3c61ceea1eaebcf56deeb8c1af442beb446f29d12c.mp3"}, {"text": "Change all of the attributes to what is relevant for your project.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b4190bac8c5216aef5d756058116c9fb1dbb2b10f2b79de0db6787e208838fcc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.48], [6, 1.48, 1.62], [7, 1.62, 1.76], [8, 1.76, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.44], [10, 2.44, 2.56], [11, 2.56, 2.98]]}, {"text": "``` ruby angora.gemspec spec.authors = [“Kevin Coleman”] spec.email = [“kevin.coleman@gatech.edu”] spec.summary = %q{TODO: Get notifications when a new object is created.} spec.description = %q{TODO: Angora hooks into ActiveMailer to send off an email notification with all of the spec.homepage = “https://github.com/KevinColemanInc/angora”", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d81b155a692b071af9c5cf20c0fb62959e8e5bec5649acfa12911f830337cb33.mp3"}, {"text": "and I need to require it in the gem file, so it loads with the gem.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6927fd144df40be44060136d60aac13ecc7e676942602e3e45006cfb963a34b8.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.18, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.6], [4, 0.6, 0.98], [5, 0.98, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.38], [7, 1.38, 1.5], [8, 1.5, 1.68], [9, 1.68, 2.0], [11, 2.46, 2.6], [12, 2.6, 2.86], [13, 2.86, 3.1], [14, 3.1, 3.24], [15, 3.24, 3.44]]}, {"text": "``` ruby lib/angora.rb require “active_record”", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/48ad4320b3412147e6cbb17cc82be867d84f9cc7e87aa2b48069e67264875b3e.mp3"}, {"text": "This will verify that a notification has been sent when the user is created.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/2a6e60bb36e40eb6e7305d3e9005a4730b12e5d0be3af4d84cc07b467537a801.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.76], [3, 0.76, 1.04], [4, 1.04, 1.14], [5, 1.14, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.96], [7, 1.96, 2.12], [8, 2.12, 2.46], [9, 2.46, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.0], [11, 3.0, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.44], [13, 3.44, 3.84]]}, {"text": "For this test to run, we will need to create the spec_helper.rb file.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9e82ab71233b84d09580f893e05e674cc8fafccd2655eb0f4fbd36d3a8ac64d9.mp3"}, {"text": "``` ruby spec/lib/angora_spec.rb linenos:true require ‘angora’", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/7741971f7200331e1009e918e5fc85fe3c8db1b5ec35831c2f07fe4ada7b8065.mp3"}, {"text": "ActiveRecord::Base.establish_connection(:adapter => “sqlite3”, :database => File.dirname(FILE) + “/angora.sqlite3”)", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9431360f357bf58d3d1b248c1e58e4d485d143b6410a4f88eb1e38835d3c27d3.mp3"}, {"text": "load File.dirname(FILE) + ‘/support/schema.rb’ load File.dirname(FILE) + ‘/support/models.rb’", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d6f24e4685555b83ae2c08b52a40ce9bce447fa0a8a5af05cd3a10ec69d55661.mp3"}, {"text": "Create the schema file like above.", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fc04c5d5d56b61bd30357ff4d724fcc2009a8746b9fa0347b514e7f3a9ad3374.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.54], [3, 0.78, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.3], [5, 1.3, 1.58]]}, {"text": "Because this is just for testing, I am only creating one model and only giving it one attribute, name.", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c7505402dff6be147dd1acb78a3d45b39b0398ea3dcf7d1fde5f1a3579b2184f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.4], [8, 2.12, 2.32], [9, 2.32, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.9], [11, 2.9, 3.28], [12, 3.28, 3.56], [13, 3.56, 3.78], [14, 3.78, 4.0], [15, 4.0, 4.2], [16, 4.2, 4.44], [17, 4.44, 4.94], [18, 4.94, 5.5]]}, {"text": "We will also have to create the user model class.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c7e642afb85a58ed5837bb2abb781e3eb86b2a843e32478fed06a9182c3ad9cc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 1.0], [5, 1.0, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.78], [8, 1.78, 2.06], [9, 2.06, 2.4]]}, {"text": "```ruby spec/support/schema.rb class Post < ActiveRecord::Base", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e562275d248abfc201c271a27183bca8dcf8659b39124b65d7be2324174977d7.mp3"}, {"text": "end ```", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/6dde54cfc20bbee1bf99675dce516f3dff5977f2737d4e17f015f20bf3d7c9bd.mp3"}]}